\newlabel{fig:vi_curves}{{3}{4}{IEC very-inverse time-current characteristic for three TMS values. The orange shaded band is the HIF inverse-time window. Within this window, the fixed TMS ($= 0.12$, solid blue) produces multi-second clearance. The adaptive law reduces TMS proportionally, shortening clearance time within the operative window. Both curves coincide in the instantaneous regime ($M > 1.77$)}{figure.3}{}}
